## 5. Repository, entity, mappers

### Repository
`OwnerRepository.save` interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` (line 75).

Active JPA impl (`@Profile("jpa")`): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `save` (lines 100-108):
```java
    @Override
    public void save(Owner owner) {
        if (owner.getId() == null) {
            this.em.persist(owner);
        } else {
            this.em.merge(owner);
        }
    }
```
`findAll()` (lines 110-115) runs `SELECT owner FROM Owner owner`. A separate JDBC impl also exists (`repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `@Profile("jdbc")`) but is not the default.

### Entity lifecycle
- `Owner` extends `Person` extends `BaseEntity`. `BaseEntity` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/BaseEntity.java`) has `@Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)` and `isNew()` = `id == null`. New owners are inserted (persist), so ID is DB-generated.
- **No `@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate`/`@PostLoad` callbacks and no `@EntityListeners` anywhere.**
- **No `ApplicationEvent` / `publishEvent`** — the only "event"-like side-effect is the SLF4J `AUDIT.info(...)` log line in the controller.

### Entity validation constraints (also enforced on flush)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`:
- `address` `@NotEmpty` (43); `city` `@NotEmpty` (46); `telephone` `@NotEmpty @Pattern("^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$")` (49-52); `email` `@Email` (55); `postcode` `@Pattern("^[0-9]{4}$")` (65).
- `Person`: `firstName` `@NotEmpty` (32-33), `lastName` `@NotEmpty` (36-37).
- Many derived getters read by the mapper: `getInitials()` (Person), `getTelephoneDisplay()`, `getAgeBand()`, `getCheckDigit()` (Luhn over customerCode), `getMembershipNumber()`, `getMembershipPoints()`/`getMembershipLevel()`, `getLocality()`, `getContactPreference()`, `getIdentityKey()`. Setters `setAddress`/`setEmail` normalize (uppercase address w/ abbreviation expansion; lowercase email) — so normalization also happens implicitly during `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`.

### Mappers (MapStruct)
Interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`.
- `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (line 30): `@Mapping(target="id", ignore=true)`, `@Mapping(target="pets", ignore=true)`.
- `toOwnerDto(Owner)` (line 24): adds `displayName = lastName + ", " + firstName` and `initials`.

Generated impl: `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/annotations/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapperImpl.java`.
- `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (lines 96-115) copies only firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone, email, registrationDate, birthDate, postcode (NOT id/pets/sharesHousehold — sharesHousehold is read directly by the controller). Because it calls `owner.setAddress`/`setEmail`, address and email are normalized here.
- `toOwnerDto(Owner)` (lines 24-65) copies all persistent + derived fields into `OwnerDto`, including the computed getters listed above.

